# API base. Left unset in normal development: the dev server proxies /api to the backend (see
# vite.config.ts), which keeps the app same-origin with its API - required for the recruiter
# session cookie. Set API_PROXY_TARGET (no VITE_ prefix, never exposed to the browser) to point
# the proxy at a backend on another host or port.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# There is deliberately NO recruiter credential here, and there must never be one. Anything with
# a VITE_ prefix is compiled into the public JavaScript bundle, where anyone who loads the site
# can read it.
# Recruiter accounts live in the backend's PostgreSQL database. Recruiters register at
# /signup and sign in at /login; the browser holds only an HttpOnly session cookie.
# See docs/recruiter-auth.md.

# Which speech-to-text provider the candidate interview uses:
#   azure    - Azure AI Speech (production). The browser gets a short-lived token from the
#              backend; no Azure secret is ever bundled here.
#   browser  - the browser's own Web Speech API. Recognition quality is poor in real Chrome;
#              development/offline use only.
#   disabled - no voice input; candidates type.
# Should match the backend's SPEECH_PROVIDER - the backend is what gates token issuance.
VITE_SPEECH_PROVIDER=browser

# NOTE: there is deliberately no VITE_AZURE_SPEECH_KEY and there must never be one. Anything
# with a VITE_ prefix is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and is therefore public. The Azure
# key lives only in the backend's AZURE_SPEECH_KEY (or, in Azure, is replaced by managed
# identity).
